{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q425172","formula":"H₆TeO₆","hill":"H6O6Te","elements":["H","O","Te"],"composition":{"H":6.0,"O":6.0,"Te":1.0},"names":{"en":"Orthotelluric acid","ru":"Теллуровая кислота"},"descriptions":{"en":"Telluric acid, or more accurately orthotelluric acid, is a chemical compound with the formula Te(OH)6, often written as H6TeO6. It is a white crystalline solid made up of octahedral Te(OH)6 molecules which persist in aqueous solution. In the solid state, there are two forms, rhombohedral and monoclinic, and both contain octahedral Te(OH)6 molecules, containing one hexavalent tellurium (Te) atom in the +6 oxidation state, attached to six hydroxyl (–OH) groups, thus, it can be called tellurium(VI) hydroxide.","ru":"Теллуровая кислота — слабая многоосновная неорганическая кислота состава H6TeO6 (H2TeO4•2H2O), соответствующая высшей степени окисления теллура (+6)."},"fame":26,"pubchemCid":62686,"mass":229.6,"charge":0,"smiles":"O[Te](O)(O)(O)(O)O","inchikey":"FXADMRZICBQPQY-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":null,"classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"rdkit","ref":"62686","atoms":13,"license":"Computed with RDKit from SMILES (PubChem, Wikidata)"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-0.839,"y":-0.582,"z":-0.72,"el":"O"},{"x":0.361,"y":0.434,"z":0.565,"el":"Te"},{"x":-1.034,"y":0.27,"z":2.031,"el":"O"},{"x":1.227,"y":-1.302,"z":1.164,"el":"O"},{"x":1.755,"y":0.597,"z":-0.902,"el":"O"},{"x":-0.506,"y":2.169,"z":-0.034,"el":"O"},{"x":1.56,"y":1.449,"z":1.849,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.523,"y":-1.025,"z":-0.158,"el":"H"},{"x":-0.994,"y":-0.67,"z":2.338,"el":"H"},{"x":0.623,"y":-2.025,"z":0.859,"el":"H"},{"x":1.715,"y":1.537,"z":-1.209,"el":"H"},{"x":0.098,"y":2.892,"z":0.271,"el":"H"},{"x":2.244,"y":1.892,"z":1.287,"el":"H"}],"bonds":[[0,1,1.0],[1,2,1.0],[1,3,1.0],[1,4,1.0],[1,5,1.0],[1,6,1.0],[0,7,1.0],[2,8,1.0],[3,9,1.0],[4